Revision basis: same-Run source revision cbc55917-ee06-4fc3-b46f-ff8dcca3c30a; prior PRD is archived history, not current approval

## 1. Product Scope

Deliver the approved UR as one integrated operational flow aligned with existing architecture R-04. A user or agent can inspect the bound state, obtain supported authoring/operation guidance, record actual work through the existing owners, prepare the exact gate presentation, record a new deliberate human response, apply a supported source revision and complete governance with consistent backlog/cockpit results. CLI and MCP describe the same Core meaning. The general cockpit reads and presents the resulting state and evidence. A focused decision card supports exact document reading, discussion and deliberate approve/change/reject actions, with the equal exact-text approval route.

The first increment includes the existing structured_slice and structured_delivery modes plus regression compatibility for Quick Task. The candidate corpus is bounded to the two cockpit-run collections and the assessment; it is not a general API-discovery product. The supported capability set is:

| Capability | Included outcome | Existing boundary retained |
|---|---|---|
| Observe state and applicable contracts | Current bound state, typed next operation/actor, effect classification, supported inputs/forms and exact diagnostics | Read-only inspection never repairs, selects a foreign Run or grants authority |
| Record internal work and sources | Brownfield/route, UX, approved-TP preparation/CD+Tests and required review/evidence/artefact registration can be recorded without routine control-table edits | Recording reflects actual analysis/review/work; applicable gate and seal ordering remain enforced |
| Prepare presentation | Exact eligible gate material and presentation identity/digests are prepared and returned | This is preparatory writing, not a human decision |
| Record deliberate approval | Existing bound approval command records a new exact response with operation identity, receipt and current observation | Cooperative provenance explicitly retained; no inferred/independent human proof |
| Revise supported sources | Existing early PRD revision, late structured CD+Tests source revision and the bounded approved-UR-at-SD preview/apply/recovery are described and accessible through the same owner | Only active structured SD with approved UR/PRD and linked unapproved SD is added; unsupported cases stay explicit |
| Read, discuss and decide | A current exact gate card offers approve, request change with comment and reject; opens the exact larger document and supports later exact Approval text during discussion | One canonical decision authority; no general cockpit writer, fabricated human origin or automatic gate approval |
| Complete governance | Required OR, applicable obligations, lifecycle and backlog pointer are consistently recorded or recovered | QA/UAT where applicable still required; completion neither performs nor requires Git/publication |
| Present current decision evidence | Current identifiable QA/UAT evidence, replaced history, unknown applicability and truthful version links | No fabricated historic binding, alternative QA decision or app-side policy |

MCP offers suitable operation-specific access to this set rather than an unrestricted replacement for Run State Markdown. Exact tool count, commands, schema fields and writer convergence are SD decisions. Existing adapter fields remain compatible or follow an explicit transition plan. No MCP write is exposed before its Core eligibility, semantics and recovery are designed and qualified.

Delivery stages have dependencies: shared state/operation/completion meaning; usable owner contracts and consistent authoring/evidence interpretation; bound writer flow/recovery; MCP and targeted app integration; then qualification of the complete chain. A partial stage cannot satisfy whole-run acceptance while another consumer still contradicts the same state.

## 2. UX Intent And Success

- primary_user_intent: Know what is currently true, what remains open and who can perform the next step without reconciling contradictory sources or finding hidden invocation syntax.
- success_signal: For a bound observation, current state and next operation agree across surfaces; supported routine actions use described contracts; completion and remaining obligations are trustworthy.
- primary_decision_or_action: Read the exact gate material in the card or larger view, discuss it, then deliberately approve, request change with comment or reject that version. Click and exact text are equal decision paths. Perform other eligible operations/revision/recovery/closeout only under their existing boundaries.
- input_analysis: UX_INTENT_DEFINITION.md is ready; it is subordinate to the approved UR and this PRD upon approval.
- benefit_boundary: Less search and manual bookkeeping are measured for defined scenarios. No claim that all code inspection disappears or every weaker model performs better.

## 3. Working Modes And Effective State

| Working mode | Effective state | Authority | Primary visible owner |
|---|---|---|---|
| Observe/status | Current bound source/Run revision, prerequisites, gate, actor and operation | Existing canonical Core evaluator | Invoking agent/CLI/MCP observation or cockpit current view |
| Prepare/record | Draft/registered/checked/approved distinctions; confirmed operation effect separate from fresh current state | Existing relevant Core writer plus evaluator | Invoking result and corresponding current views |
| Await human decision | Exact eligible presentation prepared; reading/discussion is undecided; card/text decision pending until confirmed | Existing presentation/approval owner | Focused bound card or equal text presentation in the agent interaction |
| Read/discuss exact document | Exact card-bound version in larger view; discussion preserves decision context | Existing exact document/presentation authority | Supported larger document view and return to card/chat |
| Submitted decision | Human intent submitted; effect is pending, uncertain or confirmed; technical tool permission is separate | Same approval/request/rejection owner and canonical current state | Focused card/result shows one decision and its actual outcome |
| Revise source | Preview causes no source change; allowed apply renews sources and dependent obligations | Existing source-revision authority | Impact preview/result and current state/history |
| Recover | Uncertain response, known receipt or pending transaction are explicit; only applicable recovery is eligible | Existing operation/receipt/recovery owner | Invoking error/result with responsible actor and bounded next action |
| Closeout | Applicable QA/UAT/OR and other obligations determine eligibility; incomplete synchronization is explicit | Existing closeout/evaluation/backlog responsibility | Agent/CLI/MCP effect/current result; cockpit shows current meaning |
| Completed/history | Governance completed; historic material remains available; no current repeat OR obligation | Existing canonical completion/evidence evaluation | Current status and deliberately separate history |

Visible state types are current observation, confirmed historical effect, registered draft, checked draft, documented approval, internal work, human decision pending, missing prerequisite, validation error, unsupported operation, transient unavailability, recovery required, unknown evidence association, superseded history and completed governance. Technical owners/components implementing these roles are determined by SD.

## 4. Activation, Blockers, Recovery And Transitions

Existing Request Activation binds an explicit delivery intent to its target/Run. Pure status remains read-only. Opening a document or changing a view does not approve or invoke a write. Each operation revalidates its exact expected state and applicable gate/source/presentation binding. The actor can obtain concrete supported-input guidance before invoking it.

Missing prerequisites name the responsible actor and applicable next step. Stale/foreign bindings, invalid seal or incompatible runtime block the dependent operation. Malformed inputs name source/field/form and supported correction. Unsupported revision/lifecycle states do not turn into raw edits. Busy/read/check unavailability remains unavailable; a supported repeat action is visible. A lost write acknowledgement shows effect uncertainty and retains original operation identity where replay is supported. Conflict/concurrent change/pending transaction requires the existing bounded recovery, not blind repetition or a new invented decision.

Transitions preserve distinct meanings: draft -> registered -> exact presented material -> new deliberate response -> confirmed decision effect -> current evaluated next operation; analysis/review registration -> satisfied internal input, not human approval; revision preview -> allowed apply -> changed dependencies and renewed obligations; failed/uncertain response -> inspect/retry/recover -> fresh current state; QA pass before approval -> human decision pending; revise/block -> owned obligation; accepted applicable QA/UAT plus valid OR/requirements -> governance completion. Completed -> history inspection does not reopen closeout.

View or interaction closure ends that interaction without approval/completion. Actual backend teardown is evidenced separately. Old asynchronous read/check results must not revive superseded state after refresh, revision or expiry. The general cockpit remains a reader of Core descriptions and retains existing draft checks. Only the focused bound decision card adds approve/change/reject actions; it cannot submit arbitrary Run updates. A user click is the gate decision. A host execution-permission prompt is not another gate decision and cannot by itself approve material.

