## 6. Non-Goals

No new authority/store/orchestrator, universal code-understanding tool, tool-per-candidate multiplication, automatic approval or altered gate sequence; no revision expansion beyond the specifically bounded early UR-at-SD case. No stronger independent human proof or blanket host/model qualification. No general test/owner inventory, product synthetic test profile, installer/restart work, general cockpit redesign or arbitrary app writes; only the explicit focused bound decision card is added. No foreign-run changes, inferred decisions or automatic Git/release/publication. Normal architecture/code review remains necessary.

## 7. Users And Roles

The human directing delivery owns deliberate intent and gate decisions. The agent prepares permissible artefacts/work and forwards exact new responses; it cannot claim independent human proof. Existing Core owners determine eligibility, recording, evidence applicability and state. QA alone makes final quality judgement. Review skills provide their actual evidence dimensions. CLI/MCP transport existing contracts; the general cockpit presents current results and protected document/check behavior. The focused card forwards deliberate user actions through the same authority as exact text; host permission is separate and AI content is never decision provenance. Operational/native-host actions remain separately attributable when necessary.

## 8. Constraints

Use existing architecture operation ownership and R-04/R-05 separation. Expected pre-state binding, durable effect and observed post-state remain distinct. Per-operation repeatability must be qualified; no generic arbitrary-Run writer. Keep source revisions, historical presentations/approvals/receipts and foreign Runs protected. Unsupported lifecycle states remain explicit. SD must resolve mandatory compatibility/recovery/formats/current-evidence questions before implementation planning. The formerly observed different runtimes remain historical; refreshed installed/loaded MCP digest 04b79e75931e64d4b2bacca6af48a5e5dec48d52d5b4c0a329e041957c86f65c now verifies the bootstrap history, not the unimplemented integrated writers/native card. No digest equality alone qualifies a host. One Run does not mean one unstructured change or one test.

## 9. Evidence Requirements

Maintain a fixed baseline corpus from EVIDENCE_BROWNFIELD.md and the two candidate collections. Real writes use disposable targets, never live reference approvals. Include focused card/read/discussion/text/permission/concurrency cases, the bounded early UR-at-SD renewal, renewed UX/source and non-revised flows, all specified recording/presentation/decision/revision boundaries, Quick Task and both structured modes, historical receipts/evidence, stale/foreign binding, lost acknowledgement, payload conflict, concurrency and interrupted backlog synchronization. Compare same-bound Core/CLI/MCP/app meanings; trace every criterion through SD/TP rather than creating a second acceptance register.

For supported routine corpus, separately count undocumented invocation/parser searches, hand-edits, rejected schema calls, false follow-ups, redundant continuation prompts and successful recovery. Preserve legitimate approval/external-action counts and negative checks. Keep model, runtime and host fixed where a before/after claim needs comparability; otherwise report differences, not a performance conclusion. Synthetic tests establish contract/recovery evidence, not measured model or native-host quality.

Qualification must state actual commit/build/package/resource identity, installed MCP path, protocol exercise and any required native interaction/teardown observation. Later candidate changes invalidate only dependent evidence with applicability explained. Every changed localized presentation has a rendered matrix for all registered languages. No QA pass, completion or release is implied by this draft.

## 10. Risks And Open Questions

The main risk is exposing inconsistent or incomplete Core behavior more widely through MCP. A second mapping/parser/policy is not an acceptable fix. SD must decide complete proposed/persisted state preparation, typed operations, exact capabilities/tool shape, compatible legacy writer convergence, operation-specific retry/locking/receipt recovery, multi-record closeout, authoring interpretation and current-evidence applicability. Unknown historical association must remain honest. Product scope and acceptance above are concrete; technical decisions are owned deferrals below.

Related active scopes remain independent. Reuse the current repository baseline and recheck shared-owner changes during TP preparation. No retrospective completion or approval is owed to another Run. Native acceptance requires an actual user card decision and exact larger-view/accessibility/session observations; prepare candidate and actions before asking. A text response alone is insufficient for the new click capability. Broad installer remediation and independent host enforcement remain excluded.

